<title>NETHERLANDS: ACF CHAIRMAN TO STEP DOWN AFTER AGM.</title>
<headline>ACF CHAIRMAN TO STEP DOWN AFTER AGM.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>ACF Holding NV said its chairman A.P. Blom would leave the company after the next annual meeting of shareholders on April 25.</p>
<p>The announcement coincided with the disclosure by ACF Holding of plans to increase efficiency by regrouping its businesses into three clusters: pharmaceutical wholesaling, production and other activities.</p>
<p>The company said that Blom accepted that this was a logical step for ACF Holding but added that it did not fit in with his own ambitions and career plans.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
